    define('DISALLOW_FILE_EDIT', true);\\n    define('WP_POST_REVISIONS', 5);\\n    define('AUTOSAVE_INTERVAL', 120);\\n    define('FORCE_SSL_ADMIN', true);\\n    define('WP_MEMORY_LIMIT', '256M');\\n4.3 Change table prefix from default wp_ during install (hoa_ example).\\n4.4 Limit login attempts (SG Security covers).\\n4.5 Install Wordfence only if SG Security deemed insufficient (skip to reduce duplication).\\n\\n5. Theme & Child Theme\\n5.1 Install “GeneratePress” (free, lightweight, accessible).\\n5.2 Create child theme:\\n    wp --allow-root scaffold child-theme dunbaroakshoa-child --parent_theme=generatepress --theme_name=\\\"Dunbar Oaks HOA Child\\\"\\n5.3 Add custom logo / colors later via Customizer; no branding exists now – use neutral palette (#004d40 teal accents, Sans-Serif fonts).\\n\\n6. Plugins – Install & Configure\\n6.1 SG Optimizer (auto-installed).\\n6.2 Simple Membership – manage members, restrict pages.\\n6.3 User Role Editor – create “Resident” (read), “Board” (edit_others_pages, edit_pages, upload_files).\\n6.4 WP Mail SMTP – SMTP host: <smtp.mailgun.org> or SiteGround mail; set From address.\\n6.5 UpdraftPlus – schedule daily backups to Google Drive bucket <gdrive-folder-id>.\\n6.6 Contact Form 7 – HOA contact form.\\n6.7 Redirection – manage 301s if page structure changes.\\n6.8 Disable Comments (optional).\\n6.9 Activate & configure each.\\n\\n7. Membership & Role Setup\\n7.1 User Role Editor → Add role “Resident” (clone Subscriber).\\n7.2 Add role “Board” (clone Editor, but remove edit_theme_options).\\n7.3 Simple Membership → Settings:\\n    • Enable WP user integration.\\n    • Membership levels:\\n        – Resident (Level ID 2) ➜ Access to protected pages.\\n        – Board (Level ID 3) ➜ Same as Resident + backend editing.\\n7.4 Registration: Disable public self-registration. Admin imports users.\\n7.5 Import Users:\\n    • Prepare CSV: email, first_name, last_name, address, membership_level_id.\\n    • Use Simple Membership “Bulk Member Import” tool.\\n    • Residents receive activation email via SMTP.\\n\\n8. Protected Pages Implementation\\n8.1 Create pages: Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events.\\n8.2 For each page → Simple Membership Protection meta-box ➜ check “Members only” (Resident + Board).\\n8.3 Nav Menu: Appearance → Menus → Add above pages. Menu Visibility Plugin (optional) to hide menu items until logged-in.\\n8.4 Create landing page “Resident Login” with /login shortcode from Simple Membership.\\n\\n9. Content Update Workflow (Non-Technical)\\n9.1 Use Gutenberg Block Editor; provide quick-edit doc (see Section 12).\\n9.2 For News posts: categorize as “News & Events”; create menu link to /category/news-events.\\n9.3 Board members edit pages via Pages → Edit.\\n9.4 Media uploads via Media Library (max 2 MB; enforce via SG Optimizer).\\n\\n10. Email & SMTP\\n10.1 Create mailbox noreply@dunbaroakshoa.com in Site Tools → Email.\\n10.2 WP Mail SMTP → Configure mailer, host smtp.siteground.net, TLS 587.\\n10.3 Send test email.\\n\\n11. Backups & Rollback\\n11.1 SG automatic daily backup (retain 30 copies).\\n11.2 UpdraftPlus to Google Drive – schedule daily, retain 15 copies.\\n11.3 Manual snapshot before plugin/theme updates: Site Tools → Backup → Create.\\nRollback Path:\\n    a) Minor WP error → SG Backup Restore to prior day.\\n    b) Major compromise → Provision clean SG instance, restore UpdraftPlus backup, rotate all creds.\\n\\n12. Hand-Off Documentation\\n12.1 Create HOA-Site-Admin-Guide.pdf with login procedure, adding/removing residents, posting news, restoring backups.\\n12.2 Store PDF in /wp-content/uploads/docs/ and share via Google Drive.\\n\\n13. GDPR/US Privacy Notes\\n13.1 Simple Membership stores PII; enable Data Export/Erase in WP privacy settings.\\n13.2 Add Privacy Policy page; link in footer.\\n13.3 Use reCAPTCHA on Contact Form 7.\\n13.4 Honor unsubscribe & data deletion upon request.\\n\\n14. Testing Checklist\\n14.1 Anonymous visitor cannot access protected pages.\\n14.2 Resident user logs in, sees pages.\\n14.3 Board user can edit page, save, view update.\\n14.4 Backup & Restore simulation in staging.\\n14.5 Mobile responsiveness via BrowserStack.\\n\\n15. Go-Live\\n15.1 Enable SG Caching (Dynamic + Memcached).\\n15.2 Switch “Search Engine Visibility” → allow indexing.\\n15.3 Announce launch via Mailgun campaign to residents.\\n\\n16. Maintenance Plan\\n16.1 Monthly: apply updates, test.\\n16.2 Quarterly: review user list, remove ex-residents.\\n16.3 Annual: re-evaluate hosting cost; renew domain & SSL.\\n\\n17. Cost Estimate Summary\\n• SiteGround GrowBig: ~US$240 / yr (promo first yr ~US$120).\\n• Domain: US$15 / yr.\\n• UpdraftPlus (free) – optional Premium US$70 one-time.\\n• Mailgun 10 k emails free/mo.\\nTotal recurring ≈ US$255 / yr.\\n\\n====================================================================\\nExecution Dependencies / Inputs Required\\n• SiteGround account credentials.\\n• Registrar access (if separate).\\n• GDrive or S3 creds for UpdraftPlus.\\n• Resident CSV.\\n• Board member emails.\\n\\n====================================================================\\nEND DEP\\n---END FILE CONTENT---\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}}},"displayName":"generate","startTime":1753402468411,"endTime":1753402474020.7979}